Organization = {Appl Energy; Appl Energy Innovat Inst; Tongji Univ; China Assoc Sci \&
   Technol, HOME Program; Malardalen Univ, Future Energy Profile; Shanghai
   Key Lab Urban Regenerat \& Spatial Optimizat Technol; MOE Joint Lab Int
   Cooperat Eco Urban Design; Sichuan Univ; Shanghai Univ Electric Power;
   BEEUE; Int Clean Energy Talent Program; UNiLAB},
Abstract = {The disorderly construction of cities, the emissions of industrial gases
   and motor vehicle exhaust aggravate the environmental problems such as
   urban heat island and haze, thus imminent improvement of the urban
   thermal environment is required. Urban ventilation system can facilitate
   urban air circulation, which can alleviate the urban heat island effect
   and improve air quality to some extent. As an important part of the
   urban landscape system, the cool island effect of parks plays an
   important role in improving the urban thermal environment, combining the
   cold island effect of the park with the surrounding roads, building a
   small ventilation system in the area, which will help improve air
   quality in the region. This paper selects Chengdu Renmin Park as a case,
   and analysis the effects of different layout on the wind velocity by CFD
   method. The results show that (1) air passage disperses the air flow in
   the interior of the park; (2) but by air passage, the velocity at urban
   road where faced the air passage be improved in some degree; (3)
   moreover, the graphic and the length of the air passage has great
   effects on wind velocity. Copyright 2018 Elsevier Ltd. All rights
   reserved.},
