   Transact Ecol \& Environm},
Abstract = {Increase in public awareness toward high quality living environment led
   landscape being seen as the important component of urban environment in
   Malaysia. The landscape beautification projects of protocol roads,
   pocket parks, urban squares, promenades and urban woodland were found to
   give positive impact on the quality of life of the urban area. However,
   issue of green space availability in urban area requires new approach.
   The landscape beautification project has been now changed into more
   integrated Urban Landscape Program (ULP). The ULP emphasizes
   regeneration of urban green spaces to ensure sustainability. This paper
   will further discuss the way forward in sustaining the urban landscape
   development program in Malaysia as part of the effort to create
   sustainable cities through effective landscape planning.},
