   Tourism Chamber Commerce; Lingnan Int Grp; Chime Long Grp; Hengda Hotel
   Management Grp; Amer Scholar Press; Jinan Univ, Alumni Assoc},
Abstract = {There are more and more urban parks that are free of charge in China,
   which greatly increases people's commonwealth and social welfare. But it
   also brings many problems for managing them. This paper attempts to
   explore the perceptions and attitudes of residents towards urban free
   parks. Implementing a quantitative research approach, questionnaires
   were distributed to those who visited Tianhe Park of Guangzhou. The
   results indicate free parks are widely known by the general public.
   Respondents thought opening free parks free could raise a city's image,
   as well as benefit its citizens. Half of the respondents believed that
   the advantages of parks free of charge overweighed the disadvantages.
   Management of the free park is in order, which results in visitors' high
   satisfaction. Free parks may have certain negative effects, however,
   they can be reduced to the least extent so long as they are managed
   scientifically. Suggestions for constructing and managing free parks are
   presented.},
