Abstract = {Public open spaces (POS) are the main locations which influence the
   quality of life. This paper focuses upon the impact of street access
   improvements on the presence in streets. Dardasht district has been
   selected as the case study. In this district, the improvement project
   began in 2006. The primary purpose was to determine if there were
   changes in the reported pedestrian street use after the improvement,
   compared to before the intervention began. Questionnaire forms have been
   applied to 348 users to evaluate perceptions of the neighborhood
   streets. Finally, on the basis of the findings, some recommendations
   have been suggested. (C) 2012 Published by Elsevier B.V. Selection
