   Teknologi Bandung, Bandung, INDONESIA, APR 02-05, 2018},
Organization = {Inst Teknologi Bandung, Sch Architecture, Planning \& Policy Dev, Urban
   \& Reg Planning Study Program; Inst Teknologi Bandung, Res Ctr
   Infrastructure \& Reg Dev},
Abstract = {Several studies have shown that living close to a park is associated
   with high levels of happiness. However, there is a possible difference
   in the level of happiness between living close to a park (0-400 meters
   radius) compared to living far from the park (400-1.000 meters radius).
   Therefore, this study aims to compare the influence of Place Attachment
   on the level of happiness for people living near a park, especially
   residential parks in some housing areas in Malang City. Place Attachment
   in this study defined as a bond between an individual and a particular
   setting. The study demonstrates a positive influence of Place Attachment
   on the level of happiness of people living near the park. Respondents
   who live close to a park (R = 0.441; Happiness Level = 97.8\%; Average
   Happiness = 6.833) tend to have a higher level of happiness compared to
   respondents who live far from a park (R = 0.326; Happiness Level =
   69.9\%; average Happiness = 4.148). This result shows the urgency to
   reconsider the provision standard of residential parks in Indonesia
   which only suggests one residential park for every 1,000 meters radius.},
