Abstract = {The constant emergency of theme parks has become the main development
   trend of the global tourism industry. To a certain extent, a good theme
   park can promote the regional tourism and economic development and
   improve the recreational level of local residents. By mainly studying
   influences of Chinese theme parks on urban economy, the author analyzes
   the advantages and disadvantages of large Chinese theme parks; and
   points out several factors affecting the development processes of theme
   parks, e.g. the development level of urban economy, governmental
   attitude and policy, the cluster competition situation, economic
   distance, and traffic condition of theme parks.},
