   WREP 2014},
Year = {2014},
Pages = {469-475},
Note = {International Conference on Water Resource and Environmental Protection
   (WREP), Hong Kong, PEOPLES R CHINA, JUN 07-08, 2014},
Abstract = {The sky view factor (SVF) has been commonly used to describe the shadow
   impaction of visualization or sunshine from neighborhood buildings or
   terrains. This paper takes SVF as a factor to indicate the quality of
   open space in residential areas. Based on urban digital elevation model
   (DEM), with 9 typical residential areas in Nanjing city, this paper
   firstly realizes a fast algorithm of SVF based DEM. Then through the
   quantitative analysis of SVF in different residential areas, the open
   space of each residential area environment is evaluated. The
   experimental results show that the residential communities of Yihelu and
   Gutong lane have the best open space environment, followed by the
   residential areas of Minghu villa, Hujing garden and Jinmao garden.
   Residential areas of Changjinlou and Shanguli are the last. Analysis
   result shows that SVF is available for evaluating open space on a
   residential area. It can reflect light and heat informations such as
   view sight, solar radiation and ventilation indirectly. To some extent,
   SVF can display the environment quality information of a residential
   area including the ability of micro-environment regulation, the
   reservation of emergency shelters venue and the quality of residential
   landscape.},
