   Management and Human Factors, Los Angeles, CA, JUL 17-21, 2017},
Abstract = {Emotions play an important role in risk perception. There are many ways
   in which users' personal feelings can impact their evaluation of and
   reaction to product risks. Strong emotions and overall affect can
   influence behavior and decision-making in a manner distinct from related
   stimuli. In order to explore this relationship, the process of
   risk-benefit analysis is observed through an evaluation of several
   different activities and products, such as adrenaline sports, gambling,
   and smoking.},
