Abstract = {Physical environment of urban centres often conveys different message to
   visitors and dwellers. Psychological processes-perception, cognition,
   and recognition-guide dwellers and strangers to perceive and act on the
   particular district's functionality differently. This research attempts
   to identifies features embodied the physical environment conveying the
   district functionality. The research tools are specially designed to
   investigate the perception and recognition of young urbanites on the
   differentiations of five major districts in Bangkok. Questionnaires with
   visual stimuli are used to inquire information from undergraduate
   students. The study aims to derive the urban features conveying district
