Organization = {Transilvania University of Brasov},
Abstract = {Transport represents the second largest polluter of carbon emissions.
   This carbon emission is part of the greenhouse gas that causes the
   Earth's temperature to increase. The biggest problems are recorded in
   very crowded urban areas, in metropolitan areas and in large industrial
   parks. There are obvious differences between the cities of different
   countries, but also similarities in terms of the impact that transport
   activity has on CO2 levels. This study was carried out in the city of
   Toamasina in Madagascar and in city of Brasov, Romania. The objective of
   this study aims to identify the impacts on the environment and human
   health linked to land transport activities, for two different cities.
   The methods consist of carrying out interviews with managers of each
   urban transport cooperative in Toamasina-Madagascar, carrying out
   calculations on annual Greenhouse Gas information and carry out
   laboratory studies at the Transilvania University of Brasov, Romania.
   Urban transport is a source of CO2 which causes global climate change
   and a source of diseases relating to the lungs of living beings,
   especially human beings. This study proposes carbon-free urban travel
   using shared mobility such as shared bicycles and electric bicycles in
   order to limit the excessive use of private vehicles and make urban
   transport systems truly sustainable.},
