Organization = {Assoc Malaysian Environm Behav Researchers},
Abstract = {Fear of crimes has been led to restrictions on freedom residents and
   prevented them from participating in the public domain. One of the
   strategies to overcome the crime is (CPTED) which emphasizes on
   decreasing delinquencies by urban design and through modelling it's
   principles in public open spaces. Therefore, a survey on the perception
   of the Relationship between Support of Social Activities and Fear of
   Crime among 60 residents in Omid Residential Complex was conducted. The
   results found that the usage location, providing usage in the abandoned
   spaces and usage combination, have the highest impact on the residents'
   place attachment, respectively. (C) 2015 The Authors. Published by
