Abstract = {The article is devoted to the study of one of a kind of Perm new city
   media, such as groups in VKontakte social network (which is still the
   most popular and significant network in Russia). These media are
   interpreted primarily in the framework of the category ``urban-oriented
   media{''}, which is just entering into scientific use. Addressing to the
   largest city communities as ``My City Perm{''}, ``Overheard Perm{''},
   ``Perm Active{''}, we analyze their role in city space, their influence
   on the inhabitants of the city, their importance in perception of urban
   realities. To solve research problems, we used Popsters, a special
   analytical service, which allows to compare and analyze the
   effectiveness of community publications in social networks in such
   parameters as quantity of friends, posts, likes, reposts, comments,
   views, average percent of followers' daily engagement and so on. A
   comprehensive assessment of the involvement of the audience, reflecting
   the potential of forming communities around the media resource, is
   given. Study also shows as this modern media which ``make the city
   speak{''}, help the citizen to re-open it as a place of comfortable,
   interesting, bright living. It is based on interviews, which were given
   of leaders of their groups, overview of structures, contents and
   statistics of these groups. (c) 2019 Published by Future Academy
