   Explos Sci \& Technol},
Abstract = {This paper reports the concentrations of heavy metals (Cr, Cu, Ni, Pb
   and Zn) and assessment of pollution level in urban topsoils of Lishui
   city, Zhejiang Province, China. Pollution index (PI), integrated
   pollution index (IPI) and geoaccumulation index (Igeo) was calculated to
   assess the pollution degree of heavy metals in urban topsoil. The mean
   concentrations of Cr, Cu, Ni, Pb and Zn of the investigated urban soils
   are 34.66 mg/kg, 35.75 mg/kg, 14.35 mg/kg, 63.10 mg/kg and 191.97 mg/kg,
   respectively. Compared with the reported data of heavy metal in the
   world, the concentrations of heavy metals in urban topsoil of Lshui city
   showed lower metal concentration level. The Cu, Pb and Zn were enriched
   in the urban topsoils, indicating pollution indexes of 2.01, 2.46 and
   2.78, respectively. The PI and Igeo of heavy metals are Pb>Zn>Cu>Cr>Ni.
   The PI and Igeo of Cr and Ni in urban topsoils are low and do not appear
   to reach pollution levels, suggesting that Cr and Ni levels were
   controlled by soil parent materials. These findings indicated that more
   attention should be paid to heavy metal pollution in the process of
   urbanization especially Cu, Pb and Zn. The results of this work can be
   used as the basis for a regular monitoring program for implementing
   suitable pollution control measures.},
