   Fac Engn},
Abstract = {The emergence of low-income residential provided by the developers is
   widely available in the urban areas, which is also equipped with the
   provision of public open space facilities. This open space can be used
   jointly by the residents of the residential with various activities. The
   presence of public open space in low-income residential areas is more in
   the form of an empty plot of land and the area is not too large,
   sometimes it is only a remaining space. It is also not equipped with
   adequate facilities and supporting infrastructure. By using Descriptive
   Qualitative method, the illustration of public open spaces utilization
   by the community is obtained with various activities in accordance with
   the character of low-income residential areas. With all the capabilities
   and limitations, the local residents can take the advantages of the open
   spaces for their activities, such as religious, social, cultural,
   economic, sports, and recreation activities. Although the availability
   of open spaces located on the low-income residential areas has limited
   facilities, but the local residents are able to use it with many
   purposes, therefore they can improve their quality of life.},
