   Sustainable Development and Ecological Hazards, Bariloche, ARGENTINA,
   DEC 12-14, 2006},
Organization = {Wessex Inst Technol; Univ Siena; WIT Transact Ecol \& Environm},
Abstract = {Natural parks and reserves have to face problems concerning the
   conservation of their natural resources. Citizens and firms often
   perceive the institution of new protected areas more as a bind or a
   restriction to their activities than an added value of the territory.
   Following the principles of sustainable development, it is necessary to
   integrate the environmental protection with the needs of neighbouring
   urban areas and production sites. The implementation of an Environmental
   Management System (EMS) according to international standards (ISO 14001,
   EMAS) can support the Park administration in their complex management
   activities.
   This paper analysed the criticisms related to the application of EMS to
   parks, with particular regards to the main difficulties during the
   certification process and the benefits and drawbacks related to the
   environmental certification.},
