Note = {2nd International Conference on Heritage and Sustainable Development,
   Evora, PORTUGAL, JUN 22-26, 2010},
Organization = {Turismo Portugal; Full-Service Co; Viagens Abreu},
Abstract = {Throughout human civilisation, constructions and public works are
   usually connected to the expansion of cities, enhancement of the built
   environment, corruption and sometimes debasement. However, as humans are
   born to create, we are ready to refurbish anything defaced and to
   upgrade debasement areas remodelling them into operational parts of the
   city, once our current and future needs are defined. The paper focuses
   on the urban renaissance project in the area of Gazi, the old industrial
   centre of Athens. The area was named after the Athenian factory of the
   French Gas Company, the symbol of the industrial revolution of the Greek
   capital, now an industrial park and a cultural centre. The area is
   special for its history and geographical location. Besides, mixed land
   uses have always been noticed. However, since the mid-nineteenth century
   the Gas factory of Athens reinforced the industrial use of Gazi and
   became one of the main sources of pollution for the city of Athens,
   deteriorating the wider area as well. The aim of the paper consists in
   examining and assessing the urban renaissance project, taking into
   consideration the historical, social and economic background of the
   area, laws, bibliography and research through questionnaires. Finally,
   the paper puts forward environment-friendly solutions, social coherence
   and the protection of residence.},
