   BUILDINGS AND THIRD INTERNATIONAL CONFERENCE ON BUILT ENVIRONMENT AND
   PUBLIC HEALTH, VOL I AND II, PROCEEDINGS},
Year = {2009},
Pages = {346-353},
Note = {5th International Workshop on Energy and Environment of Residential
   Buildings/3rd International Conference on Built Environment and Public
   Health, Guilin, PEOPLES R CHINA, MAY 29-31, 2009},
Organization = {Hunan Univ; Univ Hong Kong; Tsinghua Univ},
Abstract = {The wind flow around a group of tall buildings has a great influence oil
   the habitat environment. In view of the complex of wind environment,
   numerical simulation and testing methods are introduced for the
   prediction of wind effect around the tall buildings. The corresponding
   testing velocity vector is compared at different pedestrian height level
   (0.5m, 1.5m, 2.0m) for some testing point. The result indicates it is
   reasonable and scientific to choose testing point at 1.5m height.
   Meanwhile, the simulation results are compared with those of the
   corresponding measurement, the results show that they are in agreement.
   At last, some suggestion is made for choosing testing points based oil
   the results of numerical simulation. Consequently, the research is
   useful for improving buildings arrangement and optimizing climate
   environment in urban.},
